Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:23:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Tune Qwen3 block FP8 on gfx1100

Qwen3 4B block FP8 decode was extremely slow on a
Radeon Pro W7900 gfx1100 system.

Reason:
- Four Qwen3 GEMM shapes lacked tuned configuration.
- vLLM used a default 64-row tile for M=2 decode.
- The model reached only 5.88 output tokens/s.

Fix:
- Add M=2 Triton configurations for all four shapes.
- Use 16-row tiles and gfx1100-validated N/K tiles.
- Keep configuration selection device-specific.

Testing
- Compare all four kernels against torch references.
- Confirm vLLM loads every new configuration file.
- Improve median model throughput from 5.88 to 38.18
  output tokens/s, a 6.49x speedup.

Tools used:
- GPT-5.6 Sol: coding agent

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
